      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense to acquire the `blk_sub_page_limit_lock` mutex here?\n\nI wonder if there is a potential race condition. Let\u0027s say you have 2 threads calling into these APIs, and both Thread 1 and 2 pass the early check in `blk_enable_sub_page_limits`, `blk_nr_sub_page_limit_queues` will be then equal to 2.\n\nNow, if Thread 1 calls into `blk_disable_sub_page_limits()`, `lim-\u003esub_page_limits` will be set to false and `blk_nr_sub_page_limit_queues` will be equal to 1. If a second thread then calls into `blk_disable_sub_page_limits()`, it would not pass the early check and `blk_nr_sub_page_limit_queues` would never be equal to 0 (and thus `blk_sub_page_limits` would not be unset). \n\nWdyt?",
      "revId": "137a756ff244adc941723e3835b9bbb4c404f2d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
